text.en:
Goods transported under customs transit shall, as far as possible, be conveyed in a sealable transport unit -

(a) and where goods in customs transit are conveyed in a sealable transport unit, the customs authority may allow the original shipper seal to means of securing the sealable transport unit;

(b) and where goods in customs transit are not conveyed in a sealable transport unit, the officer of customs at the office of departure shall affix relevant markings or seals on individual packages for the purpose of identification of the goods by the customs authority at the office of provision.
